<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix: Proof of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ Irreducible Approximation Error of Global Linear Model. ‣ 2.2 Learning Behavior of Associative Recall ‣ 2 Beyond Local Constant Estimate ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. with <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> supported on a bounded domain <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with density <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\;=\;f(X_{i})+\varepsilon_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}},\qquad\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}\mid X_{i}]=0,\ \ \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}^{2}\mid X_{i}]=\sigma^{2}(X_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\;=\;f(X_{i})+\varepsilon_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}},\qquad\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}\mid X_{i}]=0,\ \ \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}^{2}\mid X_{i}]=\sigma^{2}(X_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The global linear estimator at <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)=\widehat{\theta}^{\top}(1,x^{\top})^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)=\widehat{\theta}^{\top}(1,x^{\top})^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes the empirical squared loss over the global affine class.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be a bounded, compactly supported, radially symmetric kernel with <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int K(u)\,du=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int K(u)\,du=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For a symmetric p.d. bandwidth matrix <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=H_{n}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=H_{n}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> with a constant condition-number upper bound <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{H}(u)\;:=\;|H|^{-1/2}\,K(H^{-1/2}u),\qquad\|H\|\to 0,\qquad n|H|^{1/2}\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{H}(u)\;:=\;|H|^{-1/2}\,K(H^{-1/2}u),\qquad\|H\|\to 0,\qquad n|H|^{1/2}\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The NW estimator at <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\;=\;\frac{\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{Y}}{\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒀</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\;=\;\frac{\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{Y}}{\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W:=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(K_{H}(X_{i}-x)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.072em;" width="2.072em"><mi>Diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W:=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(K_{H}(X_{i}-x)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{1}:=(1,\ldots,1)^{\top}\!\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{1}:=(1,\ldots,1)^{\top}\!\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}:=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}:=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To make the analysis easier, we assume the following smoothness requirements.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The domain <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> boundary (defined as <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D</annotation></semantics></math>) with principal curvatures uniformly bounded by <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The density function <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in C^{1}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in C^{1}(D)</annotation></semantics></math>. For all dimensions <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\ldots,d_{y}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\ldots,d_{y}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}\in C^{2}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}\in C^{2}(D)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the variance function <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.Thmassumption2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{j}\in C(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{j}\in C(D)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We also assume that the kernel <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> has easy-to-handle support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is radial, compactly supported in the unit ball <math id="A1.Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{d}:=\{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:||u||\leq 1\}=:\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{d}:=\{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:||u||\leq 1\}=:\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout, <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes expectation with respect to the randomness of the training sample <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{n}:=\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{n}:=\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}(\cdot)\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}(\cdot)\,dx</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Lebesgue integral over the spatial domain <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Because</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\|\widehat{f}(x)-f(x)\|^{2}\,dx\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{d_{y}}\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{j}(x)-f_{j}(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\|\widehat{f}(x)-f(x)\|^{2}\,dx\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{d_{y}}\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{j}(x)-f_{j}(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">the output dimension <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> only induces a summation across components and does not affect the order; hence, without loss of generality, we take <math id="A1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{y}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{y}=1</annotation></semantics></math> below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Integral Error Estimation of Global Linear Regression</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the global affine class</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\;:=\;\bigl\{\,g_{\theta}(x)=\beta_{0}+\beta^{\top}x\;:\;\theta=(\beta_{0},\beta^{\top})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1+d}\,\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\;:=\;\bigl\{\,g_{\theta}(x)=\beta_{0}+\beta^{\top}x\;:\;\theta=(\beta_{0},\beta^{\top})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1+d}\,\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\notin\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\notin\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{D}^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{D}^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\;\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;\right]\;\geq\;A_{D}^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.113em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\;\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;\right]\;\geq\;A_{D}^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(D,dx):=\{h:D\to\mathbb{R}\ \text{with}\ \int_{D}h(x)^{2}\,dx&lt;\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(D,dx):=\{h:D\to\mathbb{R}\ \text{with}\ \int_{D}h(x)^{2}\,dx&lt;\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math> endowed with inner product <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle h_{1},h_{2}\rangle=\int_{D}h_{1}(x)h_{2}(x)\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle h_{1},h_{2}\rangle=\int_{D}h_{1}(x)h_{2}(x)\,dx</annotation></semantics></math>. The set <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite-dimensional linear subspace and hence closed in <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(D,dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(D,dx)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Projection Theorem, the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(D,dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(D,dx)</annotation></semantics></math>-orthogonal projection of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is unique:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\dagger}\in\arg\min_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\;\|f-g\|_{L^{2}(D)}^{2}\;=\;\arg\min_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\;\int_{D}\bigl(f(x)-g(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\dagger}\in\arg\min_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\;\|f-g\|_{L^{2}(D)}^{2}\;=\;\arg\min_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\;\int_{D}\bigl(f(x)-g(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{D}^{\star}:=\|f-g^{\dagger}\|_{L^{2}(D)}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{D}^{\star}:=\|f-g^{\dagger}\|_{L^{2}(D)}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\notin\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\notin\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-g^{\dagger}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-g^{\dagger}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(D)</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{D}^{\star}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{D}^{\star}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix an arbitrary realization <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{n}:=(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{n}:=(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(\cdot;\mathcal{S}_{n})\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(\cdot;\mathcal{S}_{n})\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimality of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x;\mathcal{S}_{n})-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;\geq\;\inf_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\int_{D}\bigl(g(x)-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;=\;A_{D}^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\bigl(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x;\mathcal{S}_{n})-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;\geq\;\inf_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\int_{D}\bigl(g(x)-f(x)\bigr)^{2}\,dx\;=\;A_{D}^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This inequality holds for every sample <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking expectation over the training data proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we will estimate the point-wise mean-squared-error of NW estimator, whose expressions are given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-f(x)\right)^{2}\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-f(x)\right)^{2}\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-f(x)\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]\right)^{2}}_{\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)^{2}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]\right)^{2}\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]}_{\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-f(x)\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]\right)^{2}}_{\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)^{2}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)-\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]\right)^{2}\mid\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right]}_{\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When estimating at <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, the kernel <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the translated domain <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D-x)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math> via the scaling <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The mapped set differs depending on whether <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the interior of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> or near <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D</annotation></semantics></math>. This geometric difference drives a larger boundary error for <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NW</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NW}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will underlie the performance gap between <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NW</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NW}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LL}</annotation></semantics></math>. We formalize the mapped kernel domain and the boundary layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exact kernel domain and boundary layer.)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math> and bandwidth <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, the exact kernel domain is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{x,H}:=H^{-1/2}(D-x)\cap\mathrm{supp}(K)=\{u\in\mathbb{B}^{d}:x+H^{1/2}u\in D\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x,H}:=H^{-1/2}(D-x)\cap\mathrm{supp}(K)=\{u\in\mathbb{B}^{d}:x+H^{1/2}u\in D\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the boundary layer by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(H):=\{\,x\in D:\ D_{x,H}\neq\mathrm{supp}(K)\,\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(H):=\{\,x\in D:\ D_{x,H}\neq\mathrm{supp}(K)\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following kernel-moment shorthands.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exact kernel moments)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math> and bandwidth <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}K(u)\,du,\qquad\mu_{1}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}u\,K(u)\,du,\qquad\mu_{2}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}uu^{\top}K(u)\,du." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}K(u)\,du,\qquad\mu_{1}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}u\,K(u)\,du,\qquad\mu_{2}^{\star}(x,H):=\int_{D_{x,H}}uu^{\top}K(u)\,du.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define normalized moments <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{r}^{\star}(x,H):=\mu^{\star}_{r}(x,H)/\mu^{\star}_{0}(x,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{r}^{\star}(x,H):=\mu^{\star}_{r}(x,H)/\mu^{\star}_{0}(x,H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then we are ready to estimate the bias and variance using <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\nabla f(x)^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|),\quad\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\nabla f(x)^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|),\quad\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">uniformly for all <math id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n}:=\{H=h^{2}B:h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}],B\succ 0,|B|=1,\kappa(B)\leq\kappa_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n}:=\{H=h^{2}B:h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}],B\succ 0,|B|=1,\kappa(B)\leq\kappa_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;b&lt;a&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;b&lt;a&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Defining <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}:=(f(X_{1}),\ldots f(X_{n}))^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}:=(f(X_{1}),\ldots f(X_{n}))^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any fixed point <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}\bm{1}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-f(x_{0})\bm{1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}\bm{1}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-f(x_{0})\bm{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0}),\quad n^{-1}\bm{1}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-f(x_{0})\bm{1})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})(f(X_{i})-f(x_{0}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0}),\quad n^{-1}\bm{1}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-f(x_{0})\bm{1})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})(f(X_{i})-f(x_{0})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Chebyshev’s inequality, for any fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem 1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al., 1996</a>)</cite>, this bound holds <em id="A1.SS2.p5.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniformly</em> over <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> after multiplying the stochastic term by <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})p(x)dx}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)du+o_{p}(1)=p(x_{0})\mu_{0}^{*}(x,H)+o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)du+o_{p}(1)=p(x_{0})\mu_{0}^{*}(x,H)+o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly for <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})(f(X_{i})-f(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}(X_{i}-x_{0})(f(X_{i})-f(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)(f(x)-f(x_{0}))dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})(f(x)-f(x_{0}))^{2}p(x)dx}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{D}K_{H}(x-x_{0})p(x)(f(x)-f(x_{0}))dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})(f(x)-f(x_{0}))^{2}p(x)dx}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)(f(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)-f(x_{0}))du+o_{p}(||H||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)(f(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)-f(x_{0}))du+o_{p}(||H||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)(p(x_{0})+\nabla p(x_{0})H^{1/2}u+O(||H||))(\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}u+O(||H||))du+o_{p}(||H||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K(u)(p(x_{0})+\nabla p(x_{0})H^{1/2}u+O(||H||))(\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}u+O(||H||))du+o_{p}(||H||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(x_{0})\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\mu_{1}^{*}(x_{0},H)+\nabla p(x_{0})H^{1/2}\mu_{2}^{*}(x_{0},H)H^{1/2}\nabla f(x_{0})+o_{p}(||H||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(x_{0})\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\mu_{1}^{*}(x_{0},H)+\nabla p(x_{0})H^{1/2}\mu_{2}^{*}(x_{0},H)H^{1/2}\nabla f(x_{0})+o_{p}(||H||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(x_{0})\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\mu_{1}^{*}(x_{0},H)+O_{p}(||H||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(x_{0})\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\mu_{1}^{*}(x_{0},H)+O_{p}(||H||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly for all <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Equations <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})=\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x_{0},H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})=\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x_{0},H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly for all <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we calculate variance</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})=(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}(\bm{1}^{\top}\Sigma\bm{1})(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x_{0})=(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}(\bm{1}^{\top}\Sigma\bm{1})(\bm{1}^{\top}W\bm{1})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma:=\text{diag}(K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma:=\text{diag}(K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Analogously to equation <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}(\bm{X}^{\top}\Sigma\bm{X})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}(\bm{X}^{\top}\Sigma\bm{X})=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(x)p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{4}(x-x_{0})\sigma^{4}(x)p(x)dx}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{D}K_{H}^{2}(x-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(x)p(x)dx+O_{p}\left(n^{-1}\sqrt{n\log n\int_{D}K_{H}^{4}(x-x_{0})\sigma^{4}(x)p(x)dx}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K^{2}(u)\sigma^{2}(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)du+O_{p}\left(\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}|H|^{-3/4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K^{2}(u)\sigma^{2}(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)p(x_{0}+H^{1/2}u)du+O_{p}\left(\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}|H|^{-3/4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K^{2}(u)\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})du(1+o_{p}(1))+O_{p}\left(\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}|H|^{-3/4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\int_{D_{x_{0},H}}K^{2}(u)\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})du(1+o_{p}(1))+O_{p}\left(\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}|H|^{-3/4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})\int_{D_{x_{0}},H}K^{2}(u)du(1+o_{p}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|H|^{-1/2}\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})\int_{D_{x_{0}},H}K^{2}(u)du(1+o_{p}(1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly for all <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Equations <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds uniformly for all <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Integral Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we calculate the integral error for NW estimator.
From Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> we have that for any <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, the pointwise bias of NW estimator is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\nabla f(x)^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\nabla f(x)^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)\;+\;O_{p}(\|H\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By symmetry of the kernel <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the first moment <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(x,H)=0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Roughly, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=O(\|H^{1/2}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=O(\|H^{1/2}\|)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=O(\|H\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=O(\|H\|)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence it is important to bound <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D\setminus\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D\setminus\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx</annotation></semantics></math> separately. We first define a smooth substitute for the boundary layer <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform Boundary Layer)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any bandwidth <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the uniform boundary layer of <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha):=\{x=y-te(y):y\in\partial D,t\in[0,\alpha h_{n}(y)]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha):=\{x=y-te(y):y\in\partial D,t\in[0,\alpha h_{n}(y)]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for any <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\partial D</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(y)</annotation></semantics></math>
as the inward unit normal at <math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and
define
<math id="A1.Thmdefinition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}(y):=\sqrt{\,e(y)^{\top}H\,e(y)\,}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}(y):=\sqrt{\,e(y)^{\top}H\,e(y)\,}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that one can choose a constant <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> (independent of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>) that “sandwiches” <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, there exists <math id="A1.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all sufficiently small <math id="A1.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)\subset\ \mathcal{B}(H)\subset\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">⊂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)\subset\ \mathcal{B}(H)\subset\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the claim with <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=\min\!\bigl(\tfrac{1}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\min\!\bigl(\tfrac{1}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 1: <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)\subset\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)\subset\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> denote the signed distance to <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D</annotation></semantics></math> (positive inside <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>). For <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y-te(y)\in\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y-te(y)\in\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the standard expansion (using the shape operator <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x+v)=-t+v_{n}-\tfrac{1}{2}v_{T}^{\top}S_{y}v_{T}+O(\|v\|^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x+v)=-t+v_{n}-\tfrac{1}{2}v_{T}^{\top}S_{y}v_{T}+O(\|v\|^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{n}:=v^{\top}e(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{n}:=v^{\top}e(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{T}:=(I-e(y)e(y)^{\top})v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{T}:=(I-e(y)e(y)^{\top})v</annotation></semantics></math>. By Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u:=\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}\,h_{n}(y)\,H^{-1/2}e(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}\,h_{n}(y)\,H^{-1/2}e(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|^{2}=\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,h_{n}(y)^{2}\,e(y)^{\top}H^{-1}e(y)=\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,\frac{\bigl(e(y)^{\top}He(y)\bigr)\bigl(e(y)^{\top}H^{-1}e(y)\bigr)}{1}\;\leq\;\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,\kappa(H)\;\leq\;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|^{2}=\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,h_{n}(y)^{2}\,e(y)^{\top}H^{-1}e(y)=\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,\frac{\bigl(e(y)^{\top}He(y)\bigr)\bigl(e(y)^{\top}H^{-1}e(y)\bigr)}{1}\;\leq\;\kappa_{1}^{-1}\,\kappa(H)\;\leq\;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(H)\leq\kappa_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(H)\leq\kappa_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption. Hence <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>). Using the expansion with <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=H^{1/2}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=H^{1/2}u</annotation></semantics></math> and bounded curvature,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi\bigl(x+H^{1/2}u\bigr)=-t+u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|^{3/2})=-t+\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}h_{n}(y)+O(\|H\|^{3/2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\bigl(x+H^{1/2}u\bigr)=-t+u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|^{3/2})=-t+\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}h_{n}(y)+O(\|H\|^{3/2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\alpha h_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\alpha h_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x+H^{1/2}u)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x+H^{1/2}u)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+H^{1/2}u\notin D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+H^{1/2}u\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus there exists <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\notin D_{x,H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\notin D_{x,H}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x,H}\neq\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x,H}\neq\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 2: <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(H)\subset\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(H)\subset\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y-te(y)\in\mathcal{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y-te(y)\in\mathcal{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, there exists <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathrm{supp}(K)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+H^{1/2}u\notin D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+H^{1/2}u\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x+H^{1/2}u)=-t+u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|)&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x+H^{1/2}u)=-t+u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|)\leq\|u\|\,\sqrt{e(y)^{\top}He(y)}+O(\|H\|)\leq h_{n}(y)+O(\|H\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;u^{\top}H^{1/2}e(y)+O(\|H\|)\leq\|u\|\,\sqrt{e(y)^{\top}He(y)}+O(\|H\|)\leq h_{n}(y)+O(\|H\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">For sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, this yields <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;\alpha^{-1}h_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;\alpha^{-1}h_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>), so <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> in hand, we bound the integrated variance and squared bias of the <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NW</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NW}</annotation></semantics></math> estimator.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, we have, uniformly for all <math id="A1.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)\,dx=O_{p}\bigl(\|H\|^{3/2}\bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=\Theta\!\bigl(n^{-1}|H|^{-1/2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)\,dx=O_{p}\bigl(\|H\|^{3/2}\bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=\Theta\!\bigl(n^{-1}|H|^{-1/2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx=\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx+\int_{D\backslash\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx=\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx+\int_{D\backslash\mathcal{B}(H)}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}dx+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\mathcal{B}(H)}dx+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})}dx+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\mathcal{C}(H,\alpha^{-1})}dx+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\partial D}\int_{0}^{\frac{h_{n}(y)}{\alpha}}dtdS(y)+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H||)\int_{\partial D}\int_{0}^{\frac{h_{n}(y)}{\alpha}}dtdS(y)+O_{p}(||H^{2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H^{3/2}||)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O_{p}(||H^{3/2}||),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}(y)=\sqrt{e(y)^{\top}He(y)}=\Theta(\|H\|^{1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}(y)=\sqrt{e(y)^{\top}He(y)}=\Theta(\|H\|^{1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly under bounded condition number.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the variance, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> gives <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(n^{-1}|H|^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)=\Theta_{p}(n^{-1}|H|^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise (uniformly over <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>). Integrating over <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> (whose volume is constant) preserves the order:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\int_{D}\Theta(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})dx=\Theta(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\int_{D}\Theta(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})dx=\Theta(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ Irreducible Approximation Error of Global Linear Model. ‣ 2.2 Learning Behavior of Associative Recall ‣ 2 Beyond Local Constant Estimate ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1 Integral Error Estimation of Global Linear Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ A.3 Integral Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, we obtain the final conclusion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Precise statement of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ Irreducible Approximation Error of Global Linear Model. ‣ 2.2 Learning Behavior of Associative Recall ‣ 2 Beyond Local Constant Estimate ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, if the function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be estimated is not within the the global affine class <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)\,dx=\Omega(1)\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=O\!\bigl(n^{-3/(d+3)}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>GL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)\,dx=\Omega(1)\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}\!\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=O\!\bigl(n^{-3/(d+3)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}</annotation></semantics></math> uses the optimal bandwidth <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The lower bound for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{GL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>GL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{GL}}</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1 Integral Error Estimation of Global Linear Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NW</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NW}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ A.3 Integral Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)\,dx=O_{p}(h^{3}),\qquad\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=\Theta\!\bigl(n^{-1}h^{-d}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)\,dx=O_{p}(h^{3}),\qquad\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=\Theta\!\bigl(n^{-1}h^{-d}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H\|=\Theta(h^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H\|=\Theta(h^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|H|^{1/2}=\Theta(h^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|H|^{1/2}=\Theta(h^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> under bounded condition number). Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=O_{p}\!\Bigl(h^{3}+\frac{1}{n\,h^{d}}\Bigr)=O_{p}\!\bigl(n^{-3/(d+3)}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)\,dx=O_{p}\!\Bigl(h^{3}+\frac{1}{n\,h^{d}}\Bigr)=O_{p}\!\bigl(n^{-3/(d+3)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">at the minimizer <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h=n^{-1/(d+3)}\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=n^{-1/(d+3)}\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{3}+(nh^{d})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{3}+(nh^{d})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix: Proof of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2.2. ‣ Irreducible Boundary Bias of Local Constant Model. ‣ 2.2 Learning Behavior of Associative Recall ‣ 2 Beyond Local Constant Estimate ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The local linear estimator at <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{Y}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>LL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒀</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{Y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}:=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;\ldots&amp;1\\
X_{1}-x_{0}&amp;\ldots&amp;X_{n}-x_{0}\end{bmatrix}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}:=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;\ldots&amp;1\\
X_{1}-x_{0}&amp;\ldots&amp;X_{n}-x_{0}\end{bmatrix}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here we inherit Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and continue to set <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{y}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{y}=1</annotation></semantics></math> as in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Point-wise Error Estimation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have already derived the point-wise error of the local constant estimator in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ A.3 Integral Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>. We now do the same for the local linear estimator.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have, uniformly for all <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=O_{p}(\|H\|),\qquad\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=O_{p}\!\Bigl(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=O_{p}(\|H\|),\qquad\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)=O_{p}\!\Bigl(\frac{1}{n|H|^{1/2}}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n}:=\{H=h^{2}B:\ h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}],\ B\succ 0,\ |B|=1,\ \kappa(B)\leq\kappa_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n}:=\{H=h^{2}B:\ h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}],\ B\succ 0,\ |B|=1,\ \kappa(B)\leq\kappa_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with constants <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;b&lt;a&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;b&lt;a&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any fixed point <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Bias</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e_{1}(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-\bm{X}(f(x_{0}),\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top})^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e_{1}(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W(\bm{f}-\bm{X}(f(x_{0}),\nabla f(x_{0})^{\top})^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex43Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}e_{1}(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W(Q+o_{p}(\text{tr}(H)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}e_{1}(\bm{X}^{\top}W\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}W(Q+o_{p}(\text{tr}(H)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=[(X_{1}-x)^{\top}\mathcal{H}_{f}(X_{1}-x),\ldots,(X_{n}-x)^{\top}\mathcal{H}_{f}(X_{n}-x)]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=[(X_{1}-x)^{\top}\mathcal{H}_{f}(X_{1}-x),\ldots,(X_{n}-x)^{\top}\mathcal{H}_{f}(X_{n}-x)]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
