<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the same uniform LLN and <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math> arguments used in the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have uniformly over <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i})=|H|^{-1/2}\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})R_{0}(x_{0},H)(1+o_{p}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}K_{H}^{2}(X_{i}-x_{0})\sigma^{2}(X_{i})=|H|^{-1/2}\sigma^{2}(x_{0})p(x_{0})R_{0}(x_{0},H)(1+o_{p}(1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
