<tbody id="A2.Ex65Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\eta)(\partial_{e}f(y))^{2}h_{n}^{2}(y)c_{*}^{2}-\eta^{-1}||\nabla_{T}f(y)||^{2}C_{*}^{2}||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>e</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\eta)(\partial_{e}f(y))^{2}h_{n}^{2}(y)c_{*}^{2}-\eta^{-1}||\nabla_{T}f(y)||^{2}C_{*}^{2}||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex65Xe"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\left((1-\eta)m^{2}c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}-\eta^{-1}M^{2}C_{*}^{2}\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\left((1-\eta)m^{2}c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}-\eta^{-1}M^{2}C_{*}^{2}\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> uses the fact <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f=\partial_{e}f(y)e(y)+\nabla_{T}f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>e</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f=\partial_{e}f(y)e(y)+\nabla_{T}f(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> uses the fact <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A+B)^{2}\geq(1-\eta)A^{2}-\eta^{-1}B^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A+B)^{2}\geq(1-\eta)A^{2}-\eta^{-1}B^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> uses Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Integral Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\frac{MC_{*}\kappa_{1}^{1/2}}{mc_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\frac{MC_{*}\kappa_{1}^{1/2}}{mc_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\nabla f(y-te(y))^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(y-te(y),H)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\nabla f(y-te(y))^{\top}H^{1/2}\bar{\mu}_{1}^{\star}(y-te(y),H)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\left((1-\eta)m^{2}c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}-\eta^{-1}M^{2}C_{*}^{2}\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\left((1-\eta)m^{2}c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}-\eta^{-1}M^{2}C_{*}^{2}\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}m^{2}-2c_{*}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}C_{*}mM\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>m</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}m^{2}-2c_{*}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}C_{*}mM\right)||H||+O(||H^{3/2}||)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq C_{1}||H||++O(||H^{3/2}||)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq C_{1}||H||++O(||H^{3/2}||).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Equations <a href="#A2.E24" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Integral Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, <a href="#A2.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Integral Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\alpha C_{2}\left(C_{1}||H||\;+\;O_{p}(||H^{3/2}||)\right)\int_{\Gamma}h_{n}(y)dS(y)=\Omega_{p}(||H^{3/2}||)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\alpha C_{2}\left(C_{1}||H||\;+\;O_{p}(||H^{3/2}||)\right)\int_{\Gamma}h_{n}(y)dS(y)=\Omega_{p}(||H^{3/2}||).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The last equation holds because <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}(y)\geq\kappa_{1}^{-1}||H^{1/2}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}(y)\geq\kappa_{1}^{-1}||H^{1/2}||</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ A.2 Point-wise Error Estimation of Local Constant Regression ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, it is straightforward to show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\Omega}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\Omega}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We then show that local linear regression enjoys strictly lower bias than NW on all functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, we have <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}^{2}(x)dx=O_{p}(||H^{2}||)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>LL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{LL}}^{2}(x)dx=O_{p}(||H^{2}||)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O_{p}(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O_{p}(n^{-1}|H^{1/2}|^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly hold for all <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is straightforward from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Point-wise Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Then it is easy to prove the final conclusion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Precise statement of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2.2. ‣ Irreducible Boundary Bias of Local Constant Model. ‣ 2.2 Learning Behavior of Associative Recall ‣ 2 Beyond Local Constant Estimate ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption A.2. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption A.3. ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, if the function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be estimated is within <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(D,m,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(D,m,M)</annotation></semantics></math> where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}m^{2}-2c_{*}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}C_{*}mM\geq C_{1}&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>m</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}^{2}\kappa_{1}^{-1}m^{2}-2c_{*}\kappa_{1}^{-1/2}C_{*}mM\geq C_{1}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we have <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega(n^{-3/(d+3)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega(n^{-3/(d+3)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O(n^{-4/(d+4)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O(n^{-4/(d+4)})</annotation></semantics></math>, where both <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>NW</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{NW}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{LL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>LL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{\mathrm{LL}}</annotation></semantics></math> are at their optimal bandwidth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 Integral Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that we have <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(h^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Bias</mi><mi>NW</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Bias}_{\mathrm{NW}}^{2}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(h^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(n^{-1}h^{-d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{Var}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(n^{-1}h^{-d})</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly hold for all <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]</annotation></semantics></math>. So we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(h^{3}+\frac{1}{nh^{d}})=\Omega_{p}(n^{-3/(d+3)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>NW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{NW}}(x)dx=\Omega_{p}(h^{3}+\frac{1}{nh^{d}})=\Omega_{p}(n^{-3/(d+3)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">even for optimal <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The last equality holds because <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h=n^{-1/(d+3)}\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=n^{-1/(d+3)}\in[n^{-a},n^{-b}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{3}+(nh^{d})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{3}+(nh^{d})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Integral Error Estimation ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Proof of Proposition ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O_{p}(h^{4}+\frac{1}{nh^{d}})=O_{p}(n^{-4/(d+4)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>LL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{D}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{LL}}(x)dx=O_{p}(h^{4}+\frac{1}{nh^{d}})=O_{p}(n^{-4/(d+4)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">for the optimal <math id="A2.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
According to the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is straightforward to deduce the conclusion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Appendix: Conjugate Gradient Solver</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Conjugate Gradient (CG) method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hestenes and Stiefel, 1952</a>)</cite> is an iterative algorithm for solving systems of linear equations with symmetric positive-definite matrices.
As described in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Practical Algorithm ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we solve the linear systems with matrix <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for blocks of queries in parallel:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{i}x_{i}=y_{i},\quad\text{for }i\in\{(r-1)B_{r}+1,\ldots,rB_{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{i}x_{i}=y_{i},\quad\text{for }i\in\{(r-1)B_{r}+1,\ldots,rB_{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the FlashLLA forward algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Matrix Formulation. ‣ 3.2 Parallel Form and Blockwise Algorithm ‣ 3 Practical Algorithm ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, CG is applied within each row block, with <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{r},M_{r},m_{r},\omega_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{r},M_{r},m_{r},\omega_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> being the block quantities, <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> being the solution to be computed and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> being the right-hand side.
We use the simplest initialization <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for CG. Hence the initial residual <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to be <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Appendix: Conjugate Gradient Solver ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The core computation is the matrix-vector product <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for the search vectors <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> computed in the lines <a href="#alg2.l4" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Appendix: Conjugate Gradient Solver ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>-<a href="#alg2.l10" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Appendix: Conjugate Gradient Solver ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. The result is stored in matrix <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This operation has high I/O intensity due to the requirement to stream through the entire <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> matrix in HBM during each CG iteration.
Consequently, controlling the number of iterations is crucial for both the efficiency and convergence.
While maximal iteration number <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> can be manually set, further considerations are necessary to ensure the numerical stability and performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, the convergence and convergent rate of CG are greatly influenced by its spectral condition.
However, the conditioning varies significantly across positions. For example, for early tokens, the matrix <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is low-rank and requires relatively large <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to maintain positive definiteness.
To address this, we make the regularization <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> learnable and data-dependent:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{sigmoid}(W_{\lambda}x_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sigmoid</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{sigmoid}(W_{\lambda}x_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The dimension of the weight <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> controls the granularity of the regularization. Setting <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\lambda}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\lambda}=d</annotation></semantics></math> enables per-dimensional regularization,
though empirically set <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\lambda}=d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\lambda}=d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> suffices, where <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the head dimension.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, since the CG solves multiple systems in parallel, different system converge at different iterations.
To prevent the numerical issues from affecting early converged system, we employ an active mask that disables iterations for systems whose residual norm fall below the tolerance <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> FlashLLA CG Solver</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Variables <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in HBM, <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r},Y_{r},Q_{r},M_{r},m_{r},\omega_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r},Y_{r},Q_{r},M_{r},m_{r},\omega_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> in SRAM, block sizes <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, regularization <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, tolerance <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, max iterations <math id="alg2.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, bandwidth <math id="alg2.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           Initialize on-chip: <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d},P^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d},P^{(0)}\leftarrow Y_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            Initialize on-chip: <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{P}^{(0)}\leftarrow 0\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{P}^{(0)}\leftarrow 0\in\mathbb{R}^{B_{r}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil n/B_{c}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil n/B_{c}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
             Load <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> from HBM to SRAM.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\exp(Q_{r}K_{c}^{\top}/h-\texttt{bcast}(m_{r}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\exp(Q_{r}K_{c}^{\top}/h-\texttt{bcast}(m_{r}))</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{P}^{(c)}=\Sigma_{P}^{(c-1)}+(W\odot P^{(t-1)}K_{c})K_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{P}^{(c)}=\Sigma_{P}^{(c-1)}+(W\odot P^{(t-1)}K_{c})K_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Q}=\texttt{brsum}(Y_{r}\odot Q_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Q}=\texttt{brsum}(Y_{r}\odot Q_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{M}=\texttt{brsum}(P^{(t-1)}\odot M_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M}=\texttt{brsum}(P^{(t-1)}\odot M_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}=\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}-P_{Q}\odot M_{r}-P_{M}\odot Q_{r}+\texttt{bcast}(\omega_{r})\odot P_{Q}\odot Q_{r}+\lambda Y_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">last</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">last</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}=\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}-P_{Q}\odot M_{r}-P_{M}\odot Q_{r}+\texttt{bcast}(\omega_{r})\odot P_{Q}\odot Q_{r}+\lambda Y_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\texttt{rsum}(R^{(t-1)}\odot R^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">rsum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\texttt{rsum}(R^{(t-1)}\odot R^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math> and check convergence.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha={n}/{\texttt{rsum}(P^{(t-1)}\odot\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">rsum</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">last</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha={n}/{\texttt{rsum}(P^{(t-1)}\odot\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})})}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(t)}=X^{(t-1)}+\texttt{bcast}(\alpha)\odot P^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(t)}=X^{(t-1)}+\texttt{bcast}(\alpha)\odot P^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(t)}=R^{(t-1)}-\texttt{bcast}(\alpha)\odot\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">last</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(t)}=R^{(t-1)}-\texttt{bcast}(\alpha)\odot\Sigma_{P}^{(\texttt{last})}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta={\texttt{rsum}(R^{(t)}\odot R^{(t)})}/{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">rsum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta={\texttt{rsum}(R^{(t)}\odot R^{(t)})}/{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(t)}=R^{(t)}+\beta\odot P^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(t)}=R^{(t)}+\beta\odot P^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution of <math id="alg2.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}X=P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}X=P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the block.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Appendix: Backward Derivation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the detailed derivation of the backward pass.
Defining the following variables:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{b}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{b}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}s_{ij}v_{j}=\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{n_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}v_{j},\quad g_{i}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\hat{b}_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}s_{ij}v_{j}=\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{n_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}v_{j},\quad g_{i}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\hat{b}_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{i}^{\top}v_{j}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}},\quad\beta_{i}=\frac{1}{\delta_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{i}\gamma_{ij}{s_{ij}},\quad c_{ij}=\frac{\gamma_{ij}w_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{i}^{\top}v_{j}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}},\quad\beta_{i}=\frac{1}{\delta_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{i}\gamma_{ij}{s_{ij}},\quad c_{ij}=\frac{\gamma_{ij}w_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The gradient of the loss with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial v_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial v_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}s_{ij}g_{i},\quad\Delta_{V}=S^{\top}G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}s_{ij}g_{i},\quad\Delta_{V}=S^{\top}G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The gradient of <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is related to <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be broken down into <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> path in the computation graph.
The partial gradients of the loss with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij},z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij},z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}}\frac{\partial s_{ij}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\omega_{i}}\frac{\partial\omega_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mu_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\operatorname{Tr}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\Sigma_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}}\frac{\partial s_{ij}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\omega_{i}}\frac{\partial\omega_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mu_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}+\operatorname{Tr}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\Sigma_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma_{ij}n_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}-\beta_{i}+z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma_{ij}n_{ij}}{\delta_{i}}-\beta_{i}+z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}}\frac{\partial s_{ij}}{\partial z_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mu_{i}}{\partial z_{ij}}+\operatorname{Tr}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\Sigma_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial s_{ij}}\frac{\partial s_{ij}}{\partial z_{ij}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mu_{i}}{\partial z_{ij}}+\operatorname{Tr}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}^{\top}\frac{\partial\Sigma_{i}}{\partial w_{ij}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then the partial gradients of the loss with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial k_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial k_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{\partial w_{ij}}{\partial k_{j}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}\frac{\partial z_{ij}}{\partial k_{j}}=\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{w_{ij}}{h}q_{i}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{\partial w_{ij}}{\partial k_{j}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}\frac{\partial z_{ij}}{\partial k_{j}}=\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{w_{ij}}{h}q_{i}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial q_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial q_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{\partial w_{ij}}{\partial q_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}\frac{\partial z_{ij}}{\partial q_{i}}=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{w_{ij}}{h}k_{j}-\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{\partial w_{ij}}{\partial q_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}\frac{\partial z_{ij}}{\partial q_{i}}=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}\frac{w_{ij}}{h}k_{j}-\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">In order to compute the partial gradients of <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote</p>
<table id="A4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{i}=\Sigma_{i}^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}z_{ij}=\Sigma_{i}^{-1}\biggl[\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}k_{j}-\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}\Bigr)q_{i}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{i}=\Sigma_{i}^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}z_{ij}=\Sigma_{i}^{-1}\biggl[\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}k_{j}-\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{i}c_{ij}\Bigr)q_{i}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which can be computed with existing Conjugate Gradient solver <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Appendix: Conjugate Gradient Solver ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Then</p>
<table id="A4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial n_{ij}}\frac{\partial n_{ij}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\delta_{i}}\frac{\partial\delta_{i}}{\partial\mu_{i}}=-u_{i}+2\beta_{i}\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial n_{ij}}\frac{\partial n_{ij}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\delta_{i}}\frac{\partial\delta_{i}}{\partial\mu_{i}}=-u_{i}+2\beta_{i}\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial n_{ij}}\frac{\partial n_{ij}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\delta_{i}}\frac{\partial\delta_{i}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}=-\frac{1}{2}\rho_{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}+\frac{1}{2}u_{i}\rho_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial n_{ij}}\frac{\partial n_{ij}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}+\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\delta_{i}}\frac{\partial\delta_{i}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}=-\frac{1}{2}\rho_{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}^{\top}+\frac{1}{2}u_{i}\rho_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We denote the following variables:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}=-U+2\texttt{bcast}(\beta)\odot R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}=-U+2\texttt{bcast}(\beta)\odot R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.8" class="ltx_p">We can materialize the gradient of <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> pair and then perform the reduction.</p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}=\gamma_{ij}s_{ij}+w_{ij}z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+w_{ij}z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{ij}}=\gamma_{ij}s_{ij}+w_{ij}z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+w_{ij}z_{ij}^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.9" class="ltx_p">We omit the <math id="A4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K</annotation></semantics></math> in the <span id="A4.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">relmm</span> for simplicity, then the gradient of <math id="A4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Gamma\odot S+W\odot(-\texttt{bcast}(\beta)+\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu})-\frac{1}{2}\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu})\odot\texttt{relmm}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bcast</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Gamma\odot S+W\odot(-\texttt{bcast}(\beta)+\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu})-\frac{1}{2}\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu})\odot\texttt{relmm}(R)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\texttt{relmm}(U)\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\texttt{relmm}(U)\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Then we can compute the gradient of <math id="A4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> branch as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{W}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{W}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{h}\Delta_{W}^{\top}Q,\quad\Delta_{W}^{Q}=\frac{1}{h}\Delta_{W}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{h}\Delta_{W}^{\top}Q,\quad\Delta_{W}^{Q}=\frac{1}{h}\Delta_{W}K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.11" class="ltx_p">For the <math id="A4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> path, we avoid materializing the third-order tensor by performing the reduction internally,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=j}^{n}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+\sum_{i=j}^{n}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2\sum_{i=j}^{n}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=j}^{n}-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+\sum_{i=j}^{n}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2\sum_{i=j}^{n}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{i}-c_{ij}\rho_{i}+\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mu_{i}}+2\sum_{j=1}^{i}w_{ij}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\Sigma_{i}}z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Then we can compute the gradient of the loss with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{Z}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{Z}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-C^{\top}R+W^{\top}\Delta_{\mu}-(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu}))^{\top}R+(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))^{\top}U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-C^{\top}R+W^{\top}\Delta_{\mu}-(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu}))^{\top}R+(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))^{\top}U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{Z}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{Z}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\texttt{brsum}(C)\odot R+\texttt{brsum}(W)\odot\Delta_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\texttt{brsum}(C)\odot R+\texttt{brsum}(W)\odot\Delta_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\texttt{brsum}(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu}))\odot R+\texttt{brsum}(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))\odot U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">brsum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">relmm</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\texttt{brsum}(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(\Delta_{\mu}))\odot R+\texttt{brsum}(W\odot\texttt{relmm}(R))\odot U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Hence the gradient of the loss with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta_{W}^{K}+\Delta_{Z}^{K},\quad\Delta_{Q}=\Delta_{W}^{Q}+\Delta_{Z}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta_{W}^{K}+\Delta_{Z}^{K},\quad\Delta_{Q}=\Delta_{W}^{Q}+\Delta_{Z}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01450v1/all_results_grid_fit_seqlen1024.png" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/259;" width="476" height="259" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Test-time regression with across all input dimension <math id="A4.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and segment size <math id="A4.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Appendix: Experiments</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Piecewise Linear Data Generation.</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of segment with <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\log_{2}n\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\log_{2}n\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. For each section index <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define a sign pattern
<math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{c}=(s_{c,1},s_{c,2},\ldots,s_{c,m})\in\{-1,+1\}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{c}=(s_{c,1},s_{c,2},\ldots,s_{c,m})\in\{-1,+1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>
by reading the least-significant bits of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each segment in each sample, draw <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and construct the data <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by flipping the first <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> coordinate of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{j}=\begin{cases}S_{c,j}|Z_{j}|,&amp;j\leq m\\
Z_{j},&amp;j&gt;m\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{j}=\begin{cases}S_{c,j}|Z_{j}|,&amp;j\leq m\\
Z_{j},&amp;j&gt;m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As the result, the constructed segment is a truncated Gaussian conditioned to lie in the cone <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{c}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:s_{c,j}x_{j}\geq 0,j=1,\ldots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{c}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:s_{c,j}x_{j}\geq 0,j=1,\ldots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}\cap\mathcal{C}_{j}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}\cap\mathcal{C}_{j}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{c}(Z)=(S_{c}\odot|Z_{1:m}|,|Z_{m+1:d}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⊙</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{c}(Z)=(S_{c}\odot|Z_{1:m}|,|Z_{m+1:d}|)</annotation></semantics></math> and segment distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X\sim P_{c}\iff X\overset{d}{=}T_{c}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X\sim P_{c}\iff X\overset{d}{=}T_{c}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Training Configuration</h3>

<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Test-Time Regression.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment evaluates test-time adaptation without training any model parameters. We sweep over input dimension
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{8,16,32,64,128\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{8,16,32,64,128\}</annotation></semantics></math> and segment size
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in\{8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in\{8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024\}</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed sequence length
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1024</annotation></semantics></math>. Performance is evaluated by averaging the mean squared error over
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> independently generated sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">In-Context Regression.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fix the input and output dimensions at
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=d_{y}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=d_{y}=32</annotation></semantics></math>. For each random seed, we generate
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> training examples with noise level <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> test examples with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0</annotation></semantics></math> (noiseless evaluation). For each sequence length
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{64,128,256,512\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>64,128,256,512</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{64,128,256,512\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sweep over segment size
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in\{L/8,L/4,L/2,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in\{L/8,L/4,L/2,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> and learning rate
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{5\times 10^{-5},10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{5\times 10^{-5},10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
All models are trained with the AdamW optimizer
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>, for a maximum of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> epochs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">In-Context Associative Recall.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fix the vocabulary size <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{k}\cup A_{v}|=8{,}192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8,192</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{k}\cup A_{v}|=8{,}192</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each sequence length <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{64,128,256,512\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>64,128,256,512</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{64,128,256,512\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we sweep over the number of key-value pairs
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{L/16,L/8,L/4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{L/16,L/8,L/4\}</annotation></semantics></math> and learning rate
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We generate <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>60,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> training examples
and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> test examples each for the respective key-value pair counts.
Training uses AdamW with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>,
weight decay <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>, for a maximum of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> epochs.
Short convolution and feature map are disabled for all models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Permutation State Tracking.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fix the vocabulary size <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|=8{,}192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8,192</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|=8{,}192</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each random seed, we generate <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> training examples and
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> test examples. For each position count
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{16,24,48,96\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{16,24,48,96\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample the number of instructions
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\sim\text{Uniform}(N/6,N/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\sim\text{Uniform}(N/6,N/3)</annotation></semantics></math> and use <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> queries per example.
We sweep over learning rate <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-4},5\times 10^{-4},10^{-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Models are trained with AdamW <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>,
weight decay <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>, for a maximum of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> epochs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Additional Experiment Results</h3>

<figure id="A5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01450v1/ar_all_curves.svg" id="A5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/300;" width="381" height="300"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A5.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Test accuracy curves for associative recall across all sequence lengths <math id="A5.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (averaged over 3 random seeds). Results for different numbers of key-value pairs are averaged within each sequence length for visual clarity
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Appendix: Backward Derivation ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we provide the full test-time regression results across all input dimension <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and segment size <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
The advantages of LLA scales with the dimension <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and nonstationarity.
In practical settings, as the dimensionality increases, it is less likely to do exact query <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as in this synthetic experiment.
Consequently, kernel selectivity becomes less pronounced when noise is present in query points, limiting the potential advantages of both softmax attention and LLA compared to the ideal conditions of this synthetic experiment. Nevertheless, the overall performance trends remain consistent with our main findings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ E.3 Additional Experiment Results ‣ Appendix E Appendix: Experiments ‣ Local Linear Attention: An Optimal Interpolation of Linear and Softmax Attention For Test-Time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows complete associative recall results across all sequence lengths <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.
For visual clarity, we average results across different numbers of key-value pairs for each sequence length and plot the trajectory of the best score for each model.
Gated DeltaNet exhibits distinctive training dynamics characterized by an extended plateau phase with minimal loss improvement, followed by an abrupt transition to significantly lower test loss and corresponding rapid accuracy improvement.
The timing of this transition is highly sensitive to hyperparameters such as learning rate and dataset size.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, LLA demonstrates consistent, gradual improvement in test accuracy with a corresponding smooth decrease in test loss throughout training, mirroring the behavior of Softmax Attention but more powerful.
This stable convergence pattern remains robust across a wide range of learning rates and dataset sizes.
The marked difference in optimization dynamics suggests fundamental differences in how these models navigate the loss landscape and converge to solutions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
